{"id": "000VHK", "title": "Chaos Reconstruction", "posted": "Heute, 18:36 Uhr", "author": "varepsilon", "rules": "Play on SudokuPad: https://sudokupad.app/cl0lbkhgl7\n\nHere's my take on combining chaos construction with a jigsaw puzzle.\n\nChaos Deconstruction:\n\nComplete the left-hand grid and divide it into nine pieces, each consisting of nine orthogonally connected cells.\nEach piece must contain 1\u20139 exactly once.\n\nDigits may repeat in rows and columns of the left-hand grid.\n\nChaos Reconstruction:\n\nPut all nine pieces together in the right-hand grid, with no gaps or overlaps.\nEach piece must retain its shape and the positions of its digits within it.\nPieces may only be translated, not rotated or reflected.\n\nEvery row and column of the right-hand grid must contain 1\u20139 exactly once.\n\nRegion Sum Lines:\n\nPiece boundaries divide each blue line into at least two segments with equal sums. Separate segments within the same piece are summed separately. Different lines may have different sums.\n\nThe 6\u00d76 example below illustrates chaos deconstruction and reconstruction.\n\nFrom left to right: the starting grid, its division into six pieces, and the final arrangement.\n\nI hope you enjoy the puzzle! I'd love to hear your thoughts.", "solutionCode": "Row 6 of the left grid, followed by row 6 of the right grid, both read from left to right. (18 digits)", "difficulty": 5, "solvedCount": 0, "tags": ["Sudoku", "Region Sum Lines (Variante)", "Chaos Construction (Variante)"], "links": [{"url": "https://sudokupad.app/cl0lbkhgl7", "kind": "sudokupad"}], "firstSeen": "2026-10-17T17:00:00+00:00", "data": "", "link": "https://sudokupad.app/cl0lbkhgl7", "linkKind": "sudokupad", "settings": {}, "summary": {"format": "scl", "decoded": true, "rows": 9, "cols": 19, "cages": 0, "hasSolution": true, "features": ["lines", "overlays"]}}